(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-pour-decision :authorize-casting-pour :proceed-with-casting-pour :finalize-casting-decision :override-foundry-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799007131-cloud-itonami-isco-7131-painters-and-related-workers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the casting pour" "proceed with the pour" "authorize the casting pour" "authorize the pour" "finalize the pour decision" "finalize the casting decision" "override the foundry safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override foundry safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007211), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/foundry-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :moulder-verified :foundry-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7211"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007211: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7211 Metal Moulders and Coremakers foundry scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7211\n-- Metal Moulders and Coremakers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of\nthe rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-2 of ~17 already\nlanded: 7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121/7122/7123/7124/7125/7127/7131).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7211\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7211\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Metal Moulders and Coremakers\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed\nat `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211` (`gh api` 404 confirmed\nbefore scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote\nthe `7211` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nMetal moulders and coremakers work with molten-metal casting processes\n-- real physical-safety stakes (heat exposure, molten-metal handling,\nrespiratory/fume hazards from mould/core materials and binders). The\ncontrolling constraint for this vertical is that the closed op\nallowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes a\ncasting/pouring-execution decision, or overrides a foundry safety\nofficer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor\nis deliberately scoped to FOUNDRY SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never performs casting or pouring work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, closest domain\nshape) -- cloned and read in full in this session. The\nphysical-safety-domain shape (closed allowlist + always-escalate\nsafety flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a self-trip\nregression test) was cross-checked against\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311)\n(Mining and Quarrying Labourers) -- also cloned and read in full.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211` as an OSS foundry\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for metal moulders and\ncoremakers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Foundry\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ FoundryCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **foundry scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct casting-execution authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\ncasting/pouring-execution decision, or any override of a foundry\nsafety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- casting-batch/materials-usage/progress data\n  logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/furnace-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a heat-exposure/fume-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- casting-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ncasting/pouring-execution decision or a foundry-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-pour-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names six\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`foundrycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-pour-decision`, `:authorize-casting-pour`,\n`:proceed-with-casting-pour`, `:finalize-casting-decision`,\n`:override-foundry-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`foundrycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pour-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-casting-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-casting-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-foundry-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Moulder unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered moulder record (`:no-moulder`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the moulder is.\n2. **Foundry unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered foundry site (`:no-foundry`). Together with check 1,\n   this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/\n   foundry record must be independently verified/registered before\n   any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   casting pour, or overriding a foundry safety officer's judgment, is\n   a second HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`),\n   evaluated unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of\n   the allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   casting-execution/safety-override language wherever it appears in\n   free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a heat-exposure/\n  fume-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about foundry\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  casting-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  casting/pouring-execution or safety-officer-override attempt, which\n  is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs.\n  structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"casting\", \"pour\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a foundry coordination actor working\nadjacent to casting/pouring work necessarily discusses those concepts\nto do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`foundrycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the casting\npour\", \"authorize the casting pour\", \"override the foundry safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`foundrycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for moulder ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\ncoremaking task ...\", \"... routed for foundry safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`foundrycoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7211\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7211`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-casting-batch` that is merely\n  gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  casting/pouring-execution decision exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (molten\n  metal, heat exposure, fume/respiratory hazards), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to foundry-safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/foundry-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a casting/pouring-execution decision for later\n  automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold casting-materials\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the casting/pouring-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"casting\" \"pour\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses casting/pour/\n  safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"foundry safety officer\" only,\n  vs. also naming a second distinct authority figure (mirroring house\n  building's dual safety-officer/foreman split): rejected -- the\n  task's domain design names only \"a foundry-safety officer's\n  judgment\" as the authority figure for this vertical, so a single\n  `:override-foundry-safety-officer-judgment` op (plus a generic\n  `:override-safety-officer-judgment` alias and matching phrase\n  variants) fully covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `moulder` and `foundry` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered moulder AND independently-registered\n  foundry) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/foundry\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any\n  action\" and the established pattern from prior\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- casting-batch/materials-usage/progress\n   data logging only. Requires an independently registered moulder AND\n   foundry (`:no-moulder`/`:no-foundry`). Not a casting/pouring-\n   execution or safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/furnace-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a casting/pouring-execution\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a specific pour -- it is a calendar/logistics\n   action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a heat-exposure/fume-hazard/\n   equipment-condition concern to a human/foundry safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the foundry safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- casting-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a casting/pouring-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na casting/pouring-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\ncasting pour) or a foundry-safety-officer-judgment override -- these\ncategories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the\nclosed four-op allowlist itself\n(`foundrycoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) six concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`foundrycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`foundrycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pour-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-casting-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-casting-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-foundry-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`foundrycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a casting pour or override a foundry\nsafety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`foundrycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-foundry-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Foundry Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :moulder-verification :foundry-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7211"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)), (:test/simulator :foundrycoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7211 — Metal Moulders and Coremakers Foundry Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7211)))